cff-version: 1.2.0

title: "Genomic analysis of *Pseudomonas aeruginosa* recovered from surgical site infections from a referral hospital in Western Kenya reveals dominance of high-risk subtypes"

message: "If you use this repository, please cite it as follows."

type: software

authors:
  - family-names: Mogoi
    given-names: Nicholas Nyabera
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-5395-4953"

repository-code: "https://github.com/N-mogoi/genomic_analyses_PA_WKenya"

license: MIT

abstract: >
  R scripts for antimicrobial susceptibility analyses,
  comparative genomics, quorum-sensing analyses,
  statistical testing, and generation of  publication figures. All these
  accompany the manuscript describing
  genomic analyses of Pseudomonas aeruginosa isolates
  recovered from surgical site infections in western Kenya.

keywords:
  - Pseudomonas aeruginosa
  - whole-genome sequencing
  - comparative genomics
  - antimicrobial resistance
  - quorum sensing
  - genomic islands
  - surgical site infection
  - R

version: "1.0.0"

date-released: "2026-06-27"
